crud operations
MongoDB CRUD Operations
CRUD stands for:
Letter	Operation	Meaning
C	Create	Insert data
R	Read	Display data
U	Update	Modify existing data
D	Delete	Remove data

Step 1: Create a database
use college


This creates or switches to the college database.
Step 2: Create a collection
db.createCollection("students")


Here, students is the collection name.
Step 3: CREATE – Insert records
To insert one student:
db.students.insertOne({
    name: "Varun",
    age: 20,
    course: "CSE"
})


To insert multiple students:
db.students.insertMany([
    {name: "Rahul", age: 21, course: "CSE"},
    {name: "Ravi", age: 20, course: "ECE"},
    {name: "Arun", age: 22, course: "CSE"}
])


Step 4: READ – Display records
Display all students:
db.students.find()


Display records in a readable format:
db.students.find().pretty()


Find only CSE students:
db.students.find({course: "CSE"})


Step 5: UPDATE – Modify records
Update one student's age:
db.students.updateOne(
    {name: "Varun"},
    {$set: {age: 21}}
)


Update multiple students:
db.students.updateMany(
    {course: "CSE"},
    {$set: {course: "Computer Science"}}
)


Step 6: DELETE – Remove records
Delete one student:
db.students.deleteOne({name: "Varun"})


Delete multiple students:
db.students.deleteMany({course: "CSE"})
